<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/loyalty-rules.css?v=20261009-save-feedback">
<main class="cp-page" data-loyalty-rules>
  <header class="cp-hero"><div><a href="/admin/customers/list" class="cp-back"><i class="bi bi-arrow-left"></i> Customers</a><span class="cp-eyebrow">Customer rewards</span><h1>Customer Privileges</h1><p>Set how completed bookings and orders earn discounts on future eligible purchases.</p></div><a href="/admin/reports/customers" class="cp-secondary">Customer Performance</a></header>
  <div id="loyaltyRuleState" class="cp-state" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading loyalty rules…</div>
  <button type="button" id="reloadLoyaltyRules" class="cp-secondary" hidden>Retry loading rules</button>
  <form id="loyaltyRulesForm" novalidate>
    <fieldset id="loyaltyRulesFields" class="lr-fields" disabled>
    <section class="cp-section cp-panel lr-program"><div><h2>Loyalty discounts</h2><p>Enable the program and activate a rule, then save to apply discounts.</p><p id="loyaltyProgramStatus" class="lr-program-status">Loading saved configuration…</p></div><label class="lr-toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="loyaltyEnabled"> Enable automatic loyalty discounts</label></section>
    <section class="cp-section"><div class="cp-section-head"><div><span>Qualification and benefit</span><h2>Reward rules</h2></div><button type="button" id="addLoyaltyRule" class="cp-secondary"><i class="bi bi-plus-lg"></i> Add rule</button></div><div id="loyaltyRuleCards" class="lr-rules"></div></section>
    <div class="lr-save"><div class="lr-save-feedback"><p id="loyaltySaveFeedback" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Loading loyalty rules…</p><p id="loyaltySavedAt">Changes apply to new checkouts after saving.</p></div><button type="submit" class="cp-primary" id="saveLoyaltyRules" disabled>Save loyalty rules</button></div>
    </fieldset>
  </form>
  <aside class="cp-method"><strong>How customers earn and use rewards</strong><p>Qualification uses lifetime completed bookings and orders. Cancelled, pending, fully refunded transactions, and order-linked installation bookings do not earn an extra completion. A booking counts once even when it includes several units.</p><p>The best eligible rule applies automatically to future standard core-service bookings or aircon orders while enabled. Discounts apply to eligible service or product prices. Travel fees, repair inspections and later repair quotations, large projects, and custom quotes are excluded. Rules do not stack. Existing transactions keep their recorded discount after a rule is edited.</p><p>An empty service or product selection means all eligible items. Selecting qualifying services counts only completed bookings containing one of those services. These are continuing membership benefits once the threshold is reached, rather than one-use coupons.</p></aside>
</main>
